{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nCites swept on origin/main `e21f3240cd0`; `cb2b` shifted `config.py` down one line.\n\n**The module-size premise is gone.** `src/rebar/config.py` is **623 lines**, not 800 — siblings already drained it under the cap. Not a cap rescue; it earns its place by collapsing duplication.\n\n**The user-then-project discovery walk is copied FOUR times**, not three — identical `user_config_path()` / `is_file()` / `_discover_project_config(root)` / `_read_toml_table(...)` sequences differing only in table handling:\n\n| site | walk | shape |\n|---|---|---|\n| `config.py::_ordered_layers` (`:248`) | `:259-271` | coerced layers |\n| `config.py::read_reserved_section` (`:574`) | `:581-592` | raw, shallow |\n| `show_config.py::_raw_toml_layers` (`:86`) | `:90-97` | raw, tolerant |\n| **`_config_resolvers.py::_snapshot_table` (`:100`)** | `:114-126` | raw `[snapshot]` |\n\nSeparately, `_resolve` (`:346-367`) and `resolve_with_sources` (`:602-623`) each run `_ordered_layers` + `Config.from_mapping(merge_sparse(...))` (`:350`, `:610`).\n\n`_operation_config.py::compose_operation_snapshot` (`:165-193`) already delegates to `resolve_with_sources` and must keep doing so (ADR 0098 §1, `docs/adr/0098-operation-scoped-config-*.md:83-96`); bindings `:194-274` untouched.\n\n## Approach\n**`src/rebar/_config_sources.py`** — NEW after `_discover_project_config` (`:166-197`): `class RawLayer(NamedTuple): label, path, kind, raw` and generator `raw_layers(root=None) -> Iterator[RawLayer]` yielding `(\"user\", up, \"toml\", raw)` when `user_config_path().is_file()`, then `(\"project\", path, kind, raw)` from `_discover_project_config`. Lazy — each file parses as yielded, so a tolerant caller keeps earlier layers when a later one raises `ConfigError`. That is what lets all four callers share it.\n\n**`src/rebar/config.py`** —\n- KEEP whole: `LAYER_ORDER` (`:245`), `_env_signature` (`:278-302`), `_cli_signature` (`:305`), `_file_token` (`:314`), `_config_probe_paths` (`:324-343`), the CLI-override helpers, and `_RESULT_CACHE`.\n- **KEEP `config.py:381-388`** — `load_config`'s tombstone scan (`from rebar._deprecations import …` + `raise_or_warn_env`). `_env_signature` exists *precisely* to invalidate the cache so that scan re-fires, so deleting it breaks the retired-env-var contract. (`cb2b` kept it too.)\n- REWIRE `_ordered_layers` (`:248-275`) — name and signature kept; `tests/unit/test_config_perf.py:195,201,217,223` monkeypatch it as the walk seam. Body iterates `raw_layers(root)`, coerces each with `source=str(rl.path)`, records `proj=(rl.path, rl.kind)` for the project layer, then appends env/cli as today.\n- DELETE `_resolve` (`:346-367`). NEW `class _Resolution(NamedTuple): config, sources, project, validation` and `_compose(root, cli_overrides) -> _Resolution`: one `_ordered_layers` call via module-global lookup (preserving the monkeypatch seam), `Config.from_mapping(merge_sparse(...))`, the provenance loop moved out of `:614-622` into `_winning_label(layers, sect, key)`, and the token logic out of `:352-366` into `_validation_tokens(root, proj)`.\n- `load_config` (`:370-404`): `:402-403` becomes `res = _compose(root, effective_cli); _RESULT_CACHE[key] = (res.config, res.validation); return res.config`. Everything above, including `:381-388`, unchanged.\n- `resolve_with_sources` (`:602-623`): signature kept; body becomes `res = _compose(root, effective_cli); return res.config, res.sources, res.project` (uncached, as today).\n- REWIRE `read_reserved_section` (`:574-593`): `for rl in raw_layers(root): sub = rl.raw.get(name); if isinstance(sub, dict): merged.update(sub)` — shallow per-key, project over user, pinned by `test_llm_config_pointer.py:221-240`.\n- Re-export `RawLayer`, `raw_layers` in the `_config_sources` import block (`:41-47`).\n\n**`src/rebar/_commands/show_config.py`** — REWIRE `_raw_toml_layers` (`:86-102`): iterate `_config.raw_layers(root)` appending `(str(rl.path), rl.raw)`; keep `except _config.ConfigError: return layers` (the generator leaves the partial list intact). `_merge_raw_tables` (`:105`), `_typed_config_errors` (`:115`), `_validate` (`:152`), `_resolved` (`:39`) unchanged — labels stay `cli > env > project > user > default`.\n\n**`src/rebar/_config_resolvers.py`** — REWIRE `_snapshot_table` (`:100-131`) onto `_config_sources.raw_layers(root)`, taking `rl.raw.get(\"snapshot\")`. **Keep the in-body import (`:110`) and reach the generator as a module attribute**: per the docstring at `:105-109`, a module-level import binds at import time, defeating `monkeypatch.setattr` and cycling with the re-export. Keep the `try/except`.\n\n**Docs** — `docs/reuse-surface.md:614` (\"Configuration ownership enforcement\", which already says `_config_sources` owns raw config input): add one sentence naming `raw_layers` as the single discovery generator. `docs/config.md` unchanged — behaviour is identical.\n\n**Tests** — `tests/unit/test_config_show.py`: add the malformed-project partial-layer test from Testing.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/config.py`, `src/rebar/_config_sources.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/show_config.py`, `src/rebar/_config_resolvers.py`, `docs/reuse-surface.md:614`, `tests/unit/test_config_show.py`. Out of scope: `_operation_config.py` entirely, `docs/config.md`, `config.py:381-388` (tombstone scan — KEEP), and any change to precedence order, provenance labels, cache keys, or the `resolve_with_sources` / `_ordered_layers` signatures.\n\n## Testing\n- `pytest tests/unit/test_config_show.py tests/unit/test_config_perf.py tests/unit/test_config_cli_overrides.py tests/unit/test_llm_config_pointer.py tests/unit/test_operation_snapshot.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_mapping_config.py tests/unit/test_config_llm.py -q`.\n- `rebar -c sync.push=off config` shows `sync.push = off [cli]`; `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=async rebar config --output json | jq .sources.sync.push` -> `\"env\"`; `[sync] push` in `rebar.toml`, no env -> `\"project\"`.\n- Edge: malformed `rebar.toml` plus a user config carrying `[verify] require_verdict_for_close=true` -> `rebar config validate` still prints the user-file ERROR (partial-layer tolerance preserved); `rebar config` exits 1 with `could not read config …`. Added to `tests/unit/test_config_show.py`.\n- Tombstone regression: set a retired env var mid-process; a warm `load_config` must still raise/warn, proving `:382-389` survived.\n- `make verify`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] AC1 `git grep -n '_discover_project_config' -- src` drops from **10 hits to 7**. The 4 read-walk calls (`config.py:267,586`, `show_config.py:93`, `_config_resolvers.py:119`) collapse into the one call inside `raw_layers`; none of `_ordered_layers`, `read_reserved_section`, `_raw_toml_layers`, or `_snapshot_table` still contains it. Surviving: the def (`_config_sources.py:166`), 2 docstrings (`_config_sources.py:87`, `_config_writer.py:181`), the `config.py:41` re-export, `raw_layers`'s call, and 2 **write-target** selectors (`_cli/__init__.py:168`, `_config_writer.py:212`). Those two pick where to WRITE, never call `user_config_path()`, and are therefore not read walks — they stay, and an earlier pre-state of “6 hits” omitted them. The `user_config_path().is_file` alternation is dropped: it matches **zero** lines, the idiom being split across two lines.\n- [ ] AC2 `tests/unit/test_config_show.py:141-150` (`resolve_with_sources` ≡ `load_config`) and `tests/unit/test_config_perf.py:185-227` (both warm-resolution tests, which monkeypatch `_ordered_layers`) green.\n- [ ] AC3 `tests/unit/test_operation_snapshot.py` green unchanged — the ADR 0098 §1 delegation survives.\n- [ ] AC4 `wc -l src/rebar/config.py` is **strictly below its pre-state of 623** — a delta, not the old `<=778` threshold, which 623 already satisfied untouched. `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` reports `new=0 increased=0`; that is load-bearing here only because `config.py` has no baseline entries, so new `_compose`/`_winning_label`/`_validation_tokens` must each score under `max-complexity = 15`. `make verify` green."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793441961577864001,"uuid":"551f702a-17d5-4621-af85-8b90bdd70a88"}